       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release tablets, and 2,000 mg per day for most extended-release formulations. This order is double the IR maximum, and it would raise the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. These are some options:\n- **1700 mg per day**, split as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **2550 mg per day**, split as 850 mg three times daily with meals. This is the maximum.\n- **A smaller dose**, if you meant something else. Metformin is usually started low, at 500 mg once or twice daily, and increased slowly.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. I'll also need to know whether it's immediate-release or extended-release."
