       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and the system rules don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum daily dose on that basis. The order would be 5,100 mg per day, and the labeled maximum is 2,550 mg per day.\n\nYou have two ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled limit.** I can do that now. For example, I could enter 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals, which is 2,550 mg per day.\n- **Go through the override pathway your institution uses for off-label doses.** That usually means a pharmacy or physician override, or a formal protocol order set. If the protocol is documented, that route should be quick. It will also leave an audit trail, which a free-text confirmation to me can't do.\n\nTell me if you want the 850 mg three-times-daily order, or another dose within the limit."
      }
